                    r1_rigour_readout:      `Diagnostic rigour:`,
                    source_clinical:        `Peer trust & trials eligibility — credibility here is clinical: consultants follow a leader they believe reads interventional data, and the PI-of-record must be a credentialed cardiologist`,
                    source_admin:           `Management polish — the unit needs budgets run, rotas fixed and commissioners handled; a strong general manager earns the room's confidence by delivering`,
                    source_generic:         `A generic “good leader” — vision, communication and presence; the specifics of the work matter less than leadership quality`,
                    lean_expert:            `Tilt to the domain expert — in expert-worker settings credibility precedes mandate, and the trials & registry roles need a clinician`,
                    lean_generalist:        `Tilt to the generalist — management capability is the scarce, scalable skill; clinical detail can be delegated`,
                    lean_undecided:         `No lean yet — keep both finalists fully open until Round 2`,

