                    r3_backing_label:       `Week 8 crisis: two consultants object, a complex case threatens the submission, a commissioner wants a meeting. How does the board back the leader?`,
                    r3_case_label:          `The poor-outcome case & the registry submission.`,
                    r3_objection_label:     `The two objecting consultants.`,
                    r3_sponsor_label:       `How firmly does the board hold the line on the leader's authority through the crisis? (%)`,
                    backing_sponsor:        `Visible sponsorship — the chair publicly affirms the leader's authority, brings them to the commissioner meeting, and routes the objections through them`,
                    backing_rescue:         `Step in and rescue it — the board takes over the commissioner meeting and tells consultants “we've got this”, overruling the leader`,
                    backing_distance:       `Distance the board — let the leader sink or swim alone; if they can't handle week 8 they were the wrong hire`,
                    case_clinical_review:   `Leader-led clinical review — the credentialed leader authors the case analysis and stands behind the registry numbers`,
