                    defence_model:          `Defend the appointment model — credibility plus supplied management bandwidth, with evidenced 18-month KPI projections across performance, retention and ranking`,
                    defence_figurehead:     `Defend the figurehead — emphasise the leader's name and reputation; project confidence without the structure or the numbers`,
                    defence_spin:           `Spin the window — claim the submission was always safe and decline to break out retention or the crisis-case outcome`,
                    horizon_eighteen:       `18 months — show how the model holds beyond the window: durable credibility, retention and ranking, not just surviving 15 May`,
                    horizon_window:         `Just the window — get past 15 May; the long game is next year's problem`,
                    horizon_overpromise:    `Over-promise — guarantee a top-decile ranking and zero consultant losses to reassure the commissioner`,
                    kpi_credibility:        `Leader credibility — the upstream driver that moves performance, retention and the registry data together`,
